course: dictionary
lesson: 10775
title: Vaccination: a word for staying well
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vaccination is an injection or medicine that protects you from a disease. It teaches your body to fight that illness, so your body is ready if the germs ever come. «A girl in Auckland is scared of her vaccination» tells you it is a jab or a medicine, because you can be scared of a needle and it stings for a second.
explain: Vaccination can also mean the act of giving these medicines to people or animals. «Pets need a vet for check-ups, vaccinations and whenever they seem ill» uses the plural, so vaccinations means more than one vaccination.
explain: Context gives clues: «have a vaccination», «get vaccinated», «a flu vaccination» and «vaccination record» all point to health and medicine. To check, swap in the meaning: «a medicine that protects you from disease» should still make sense in the sentence.
fact: Vaccination means an injection or medicine that protects you from a disease.
fact: «Vaccinations» means more than one vaccination.
fact: In Britain a vaccination is often called a «jab».
fact: «Puppies need their vaccinations before walking where other dogs go», because serious illnesses spread through dog poo and spit.
fact: A vaccination protects you and others around you, and the sting is usually over in a second.
exercise: «A girl in Auckland is scared of her vaccination.» What is a vaccination? | A type of school bag | A game played with a ball | A kind of holiday by the sea | *An injection or medicine that protects you from a disease
exercise: In Britain, people often call a vaccination a what? | A zoo | A puppy | *A jab | A bandage
exercise: «Pets need a vet for check-ups, vaccinations and whenever they seem ill.» Find and copy the word that means more than one vaccination. | vet | seem | *vaccinations | check-ups
test: «Puppies need their vaccinations before walking where other dogs go.» Why? | Because the vet is always closed | Because dogs like to sleep all day | Because walking is boring for puppies | *Because serious illnesses spread through dog poo and spit
test: A girl says, «I'm having a vaccination today.» What does she mean? | I am going swimming | *I am getting an injection that protects me from a disease | I am reading a book | I am buying a new coat
exam: Which best describes what a nurse does when she gives you a vaccination? | Cuts your hair | Paints a picture on your arm | *Gives you a medicine that protects you from a disease | Reads you a story
